    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17570?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor- History",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor- History | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate/Full Professor- History Urbana, IL, United States | 1037110 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/19/2026 Back to Search Associate/Full Professor, History of Modern China Department of History College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign The Department of History at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign invites applications and nominations for the Crawford Professor of East Asian History , a full-time tenured appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, specializ ing in the history of Modern China . The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. We welcome applications from historians whose research focuses on any aspect of Modern China from the nineteenth century to the present . Scholars working on a ll thematic areas are encouraged to apply . C andidates must hold a PhD in History or a closely related field and have an established record of scholarly achievement appropriate for appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. Applicants who currently hold the rank of Assistant Professor, or equivalent position, whose scholarly record supports appointment with tenure at the Associate Professor level are encouraged to apply. Candidates should demonstrate substantial engagement with Chinese-language primary sources and scholarship, a record of original research appropriate to the rank sought, and an active research agenda with clear plans for future scholarship. Candidates should have experience teaching Chinese and East Asian history to students from a wide range of backgrounds. They should be prepared to discuss their approaches to teaching and mentoring at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate instruction in Modern Chinese history and broader East Asian history and will have opportunities to develop courses that complement their research and teaching interests. Candidates should demonstrate a record of service appropriate to their career stage and describe how they would contribute to strengthening Chinese and East Asian studies within the department, across the university, and in the profession. The successful candidate will join an active interdisciplinary community of historians and scholars of East Asia in the Department of History, the Center for East Asian and Pacific Studies (CEAPS), the Department of East Asian Languages and Cultures (EALC), and other units across campus. We seek a colleague who will strengthen this community through research, teaching, mentoring, service, and intellectual collaboration. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu. To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs Appointment Information The budgeted salary range is $ 110,000–125,000 for an appointment at the Associate Professor level and $ 120,000–160,000 for an appointment at the Full Professor level, based on a 9-month service basis paid over twelve months . Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, while also taking internal equity into consideration . The Crawford Professorship also includes a generous annual research support. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization, except for sponsorship of a new H1B petition that would incur the $100,000 fee. Application Procedures & Deadline Information To apply, create your candidate profile in the University of Illinois Job Board ( https://jobs.illinois.edu ) and upload the following application materials: 1) Cover letter describing the applicant’s qualifications and interests in the position 2) C urriculum V itae 3) C ontact information for three professional references 4) R esearch statement describing current and future research 5) S tatement of teaching philosophy, experience, and effectiveness 6) Statement of service experience 7) Published article or book chapter of approximately 20–30 pages in length We ask that all of these documents be uploaded in the above order as a single .pdf file to the “Resume/CV” section of the online application. T he search committee will request letters of recommendation and additional publications and other supporting materials only from candidates advancing in the search process. Only applications submitted through the University of Illinois Job Board will be considered. For priority consideration, submit all requested application materials by 6 :00 pm Central Time October 16, 2026 . Questions about the position may be directed to history@illinois.edu. For questions regarding the application portal, please contact 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu. Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana The University\nof Illinois must also comply with applicable federal export control laws and\nregulations and, as such, reserves the right to employ restricted party\nscreening procedures for applicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037110 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
    },
    "https://illinois.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/17564?c=illinois": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor- Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor- Psychology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor- Psychology Urbana, IL, United States | 1037114 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/19/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor Department of Psychology College of Liberal Arts & Sciences University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign The Department of Psychology at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position with expertise in or a strong potential for leveraging high-field 7-Tesla human magnetic resonance imaging with specific emphasis in cognitive neuroscience. Successful candidates are expected to establish and maintain an active and independent research program, teach effectively at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and provide service to the department, the university, and the profession. Expert technical assistance/knowledge for 7T imaging is available on site via dedicated teams of the Biomedical Imaging Center and the Carle Illinois Advanced Imaging Center. A PhD in Psychology or related disciplines is required by mid-June for a preferred start date of August 16, 2027. Candidates should show evidence of research productivity, teaching and mentorship effectiveness, and potential for external funding. Experience with magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) is required, and expertise or a clear potential to use high-field imaging is preferred. The target start date is August 16, 2027, but is negotiable. The budgeted salary range for the position is $95,000 to $104,000 at the Assistant Professor level for a 9-month service basis ( paid over 12 months). The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the experience and qualifications of the selected candidate including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. It is not typical for a beginning Assistant Professor to be offered a salary at or near the top of the full range for the position. This position will be expected to work at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign campus on a full-time basis per the University’s Workplace Flexibility policy. This position is eligible for sponsorship for work authorization. To apply, create your candidate profile through https:// j obs.illinois.edu and submit application materials. Applicants must submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, up to 3 representative publications, and teaching and research statements. Contact information for three professional references will be requested after review of applications. Only applications submitted through the University of Illinois Job Board will be considered. Full consideration is guaranteed for all applications received by 6pm central time on October 7, 2026 . Questions about the position or application procedures may be directed to Susan Maxwell samaxwel@illinois.edu . For questions regarding the application portal, please contact 217-333-2137 or jobs@illinois.edu. The successful candidate will contribute to the mission of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Illinois, where curiosity drives impact. As the heart of a leading land-grant research university, LAS brings together diverse disciplines to explore fundamental questions and address complex challenges. We prepare students for a lifetime of inquiry, leadership, and service through innovative research, transformative teaching, and thoughtful mentoring. We strongly encourage applications from those who have demonstrated the knowledge, skills, and experience needed to be effective teachers for our student population with its wide range of backgrounds and experiences, in alignment with the mission of our university. To learn more about the mission, vision, and values of the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, visit: https://las.illinois.edu. To find out more about the resources available at the university and Urbana-Champaign community please visit these sites: Benefits Dual Career Program Explore Champaign-Urbana Work-life balance and family-friendly programs Founded in 1867 as Illinois’s flagship public university, the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign empowers a global community of students, scholars, and alumni to change the world through bold, innovative research and transformative education. With a land-grant heritage rooted in progress, Illinois faculty drive paradigm-shifting discoveries, mentor future leaders, and collaborate across 15 colleges and instructional units and more than 20 research institutes. The university’s legacy of excellence includes 24 Nobel Prizes and 29 Pulitzer Prizes awarded to its faculty and alumni, $755 million in sponsored research funding, and 94 academic programs ranked in the top 20 nationally. Illinois offers the resources, recognition, and reach to accelerate your career — along with a highly competitive benefits portfolio. Discover how the Illinois Value Proposition fosters professional longevity, personal fulfillment, and a deep sense of purpose in every role. Faculty Recruitment Champaign-Urbana The University of Illinois must also\ncomply with applicable federal export control laws and regulations and, as\nsuch, reserves the right to employ restricted party screening procedures for\napplicants. Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools may be used in some portions of the candidate review process for this position; however, all employment decisions will be made by a person. This position is intended to be eligible for benefits . This includes Health, Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, a Retirement Plan, Paid time Off, and Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. The University of Illinois System is an equal opportunity employer, including but not limited to disability and/or veteran status, and complies with all applicable state and federal employment mandates. Please visit Required Employment Notices and Posters to view our non-discrimination statement and find additional information about required background checks, sexual harassment/misconduct disclosures, and employment eligibility review through E-Verify . Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act (2008) to complete the application and/or interview process. Accommodations may also be requested on the basis of pregnancy, childbirth, and related conditions, or religion. Requests may be submitted through the reasonable accommodation portal , or by contacting the Office for Access & Equity at 217-333-0885, option #1, or accessibility@illinois.edu . Requisition ID : 1037114 Job Category : Faculty Apply at: https://jobs.illinois.edu Apply Now Share Save Job Looking for more University of Illinois Positions? We invite you to search for positions at each of the University of Illinois' locations, the University of Illinois System Office and the University of Illinois Foundation. The University of Illinois System Office supports the primary missions of teaching, research, public service, and economic development for all of the Universities and offers positions in all locations. The University of Illinois Foundation is the official fundraising and private gift-receiving agency for the University of Illinois and also offers position in all locations.  Click the links below to search for other University of Illinois positions. University of Illinois Chicago University of Illinois Springfield University of Illinois System Office University of Illinois Foundation Illinois Human Resources University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign Personnel Services Building - MC 562 52 E. Gregory Dr. Champaign, IL  61820 217.333.2137 | jobs@illinois.edu humanresources.illinois.edu"
